<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title><%= title %></title>
  <link rel='stylesheet' href='/stylesheets/style.css' />
</head>
<body>
<h1><%= title %></h1>
<p>Welcome to <%= title %>.   Let's test reading get+post data</p>

<br/><br/>
<b>New Customer Form </b> to test POST request and reading data using URI  /readNameAndRespond
<br/>
<form action="/readCustomerInfoAndRespond" method="post">

  Name: <input type="text" name="name"> </input>
  <br/>
  Email: <input type="text" name="email"> </input>
  <br/>
  <input type="submit" value="Go"/>
</form>

<br><br><br>
<hr>

<b>Form to test GET request</b> and reading the data using URI /readNameAndRespond
<br/>
<form action="/readNameAndRespond" method="get">

  Name: <input type="text" name="name"> </input>
  <br/>
  <input type="submit" value="Go"/>
</form>
<br><br><br>
<hr>
<b>Form to test POST request</b> and reading data using URI  /readNameAndRespond
<br/>
<form action="/readNameAndRespond" method="post">

  Name: <input type="text" name="name"> </input>
  <br/>
  <input type="submit" value="Go"/>
</form>

<br><br><br>
<hr>

<!--
  ===================================================================
  Part B - Modern REST Version (LabFormToREST_API)
  ===================================================================
  Uses client-side JavaScript fetch() to communicate with /api/customer
  and dynamically updates #result without a full page reload.
-->
<h2>Part B: Modern REST/JSON Version (fetch API - No Page Reload)</h2>
<p>Tests sending JSON asynchronously via <code>fetch()</code> to <code>/api/customer</code> and updating the page dynamically.</p>

<div>
  Name: <input type="text" id="name" />
  <br/>
  Email: <input type="text" id="email" />
  <br/>
  <button type="button" id="submitBtn">Submit via REST (fetch)</button>
</div>

<br/>
<b>REST API Response:</b>
<div id="result" style="margin-top: 8px; padding: 10px; border: 1px dashed #666; max-width: 400px; min-height: 24px;">
  <i>Results will appear here without reloading the page...</i>
</div>

<script>
  document.getElementById("submitBtn").addEventListener("click", async () => {
    const response = await fetch("/api/customer", {
      method: "POST",
      headers: {
        "Content-Type": "application/json"
      },
      body: JSON.stringify({
        name: document.getElementById("name").value,
        email: document.getElementById("email").value
      })
    });
    const data = await response.json();
    document.getElementById("result").innerHTML =
      data.message + "<br>" + data.email;
  });
</script>

</body>
</html>
